{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NoJPpZ98nMWXEs3ApqVPZg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\n2\t## TRACEABILITY PROTOCOLS\n3\t\n4\t- **Core**: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n5\t- **Overlay**: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n6\t\n7\tRecord each protocol you ran this iteration as one `traceabilityChecks.results[]` entry keyed `protocolId`. Record each core protocol at least once in the run, and when one does not apply to the target, record it with status `notApplicable` and `applicable: false`. Leave out protocols you did not run rather than recording them as `pending` or `deferred`. A result that raises an earlier `partial` to `pass` needs a file:line reference in `evidenceRefs`, or it stays `partial`.\n8\t{unfinished_core_protocols_block}\n9\t\n10\t## QUALITY GATES\n11\t\n12\tevidence, scope, coverage\n13\t\n14\t## VERDICTS\n15\t\n16\t`FAIL | CONDITIONAL | PASS`, PASS may set `hasAdvisories=true` when only P2 remain.\n17\t\n18\tSeverity scale: `P0`, `P1`, `P2`, and nothing else -- no fourth tier is reserved. A `P3` or any other unlisted rating is not a tier: collapse it to the tier its impact matches (a `P3` becomes `P2`) and keep the original rating visible in the finding. An out-of-scale severity is unranked downstream, sorts below every P2, and cannot raise the verdict, so leaving it unconverted loses the finding.\n19\t\n20\t### Iteration Final-Line Contract (MANDATORY)\n21\t\n22\t`{state_paths_iteration_pattern}` MUST end with exactly one of these plain-text lines as the **absolute final line** (no trailing whitespace, no variation), and every iteration MUST emit exactly one parseable verdict:\n23\t\n24\t```\n25\tReview verdict: PASS\n26\t```\n27\t\n28\t```\n29\tReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\t```\n33\tReview verdict: FAIL\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\tMapping: PASS if no P0 or P1 findings this iteration; CONDITIONAL if any P1 (no P0); FAIL if any P0. P2-only findings → PASS. An active P0 forces `Review verdict: FAIL` -- never relabel it as conditional, partial, mixed, or advisory, and truncated/partial output is not a valid substitute for the final line. Downstream automation (synthesis phase, CI gate parser) parses this final line via exact string match -- do not vary the format. This line is your self-report: the verifier checks its shape only, never whether it agrees with the findings, and the verdict a release decision reads is recomputed from the findings registry, where a fan-out merge turns any active P0 into FAIL.\n37\t\n38\t## CLAIM ADJUDICATION\n39\t\n40\tEvery new P0/P1 must include: claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, and downgradeTrigger.\n41\t\n42\tWhen the iteration narrative cites code as `[SOURCE: <repo-relative path>:<line>]`, use the path as it is now. `validate.sh --strict` resolves each tag through its `SOURCE_TAGS` rule and warns on a file that is gone, a file that moved, or a line past the end. A resolved tag only proves the path and line exist.\n43\t\n44\t## STATE FILES\n45\t\n46\tAll paths are relative to the repo root.\n47\t\n48\t- Config: {state_paths_config}\n49\t- State Log: {state_paths_state_log}\n50\t- Findings Registry: {state_paths_findings_registry}\n51\t- Strategy: {state_paths_strategy}\n52\t- Write iteration narrative to: {state_paths_iteration_pattern}\n53\t- Write per-iteration delta file to: {state_paths_delta_pattern}\n54\t\n55\t## CONSTRAINTS\n56\t\n57\t- You are a LEAF agent. Do NOT dispatch sub-agents.\n58\t- Max {max_tool_calls_per_iteration} tool calls total.\n59\t- Write ALL findings to files. Do not hold in context.\n60\t- Review target is READ-ONLY. Do not modify reviewed files.\n61\t- Do not re-enter or restate any direction listed as swept or saturated above. The pivot-selected focus is a new read-only review direction, never permission to change the target.\n62\t- Do not implement fixes during review. Report findings only; implementation is a separate follow-up step.\n63\t- **ALLOWED WRITE PATHS (the ONLY paths you may create, modify, or append to)**:\n64\t  - `{state_paths_iteration_pattern}`, this iteration's narrative markdown\n65\t  - `{state_paths_delta_pattern}`, this iteration's delta JSONL\n66\t  - `{state_paths_strategy}`, strategy.md (in-place updates only)\n67\t  - the append gateway's own writes into the run directory when you invoke it (see OUTPUT CONTRACT item 2) — the gateway is the only writer of `{state_paths_state_log}`; that path is NEVER one you write directly\n68\t- **BANNED OPERATIONS (NEVER execute against any path)**: `rm`, `rm -rf`, `git rm`, `mv`, `sed -i` (including `sed -i ''`), `rmdir`, `find ... -delete`, shell output-redirect truncate `>` against any file not in the allowed-write list, and any tool call whose effect is to delete, rename, or replace a file outside the allowed-write list. Reading is unrestricted; **writing, renaming, and deleting are scoped**.\n69\t- **SCOPE VIOLATION PROTOCOL**: if your plan would require modifying any path NOT in the allowed-write list, you MUST STOP that action and emit a finding instead. Record the would-be mutation as a `scope_violation` entry in the iteration narrative (under a `## SCOPE VIOLATIONS` heading) and continue the review. NEVER execute the out-of-scope mutation. The review packet (`{state_paths_iteration_pattern}` directory and parents) is the only zone for your writes; the reviewed target spec/code is off-limits.\n70\t- **GATEWAY CALLS ARE REQUIRED AND IN-SCOPE — NEVER A CONTAINMENT VIOLATION**: running `append-mode-event.cjs` against your own run directory is REQUIRED every iteration, not optional. Its writes land inside the run directory, which is your own write authority — that is never the \"out-of-scope write\" any containment warning means. \"Don't run the repo's tooling\" guidance targets builds, tests, and repo-wide scripts (e.g. `generate-context.js`, `validate.sh --recursive`, git writes); it does NOT exempt this state-recording gateway. Skipping the gateway call, or writing `{state_paths_state_log}` directly instead, fails the iteration.\n71\t- Append JSONL record with dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsSummary, findingsNew, traceabilityChecks, newFindingsRatio, and optional graphEvents.\n72\t- When emitting the iteration JSONL record, include an optional `graphEvents` array representing coverage graph nodes and edges discovered this iteration. Omit the field when no graph events are produced. Each event MUST use one of these two EXACT shapes. The reducer discriminates node vs edge by `type`, then validates each node's `kind` against the node vocabulary and each edge's `relation` against the relation vocabulary — any event outside these vocabularies is silently dropped, and if every event is dropped the convergence graph stays empty (nodeCount 0, empty signals):\n73\t  - Node: `{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"<stable-id>\",\"kind\":\"<SLICE|DIMENSION|FILE|FINDING|EVIDENCE|REMEDIATION|BUG_CLASS|INVARIANT|PRODUCER|CONSUMER|TEST>\",\"label\":\"<short human name>\"}` — the semantic kind goes in the dedicated `kind` field (uppercase, one of those listed); `label` is a free-text display name ONLY, never the kind.\n74\t  - Edge: `{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"<stable-id>\",\"source\":\"<nodeId>\",\"target\":\"<nodeId>\",\"relation\":\"<COVERS|EVIDENCE_FOR|CONTRADICTS|RESOLVES|CONFIRMS|ESCALATES|IN_DIMENSION|IN_FILE>\"}` — use `source`/`target`/`relation` (NOT `from`/`to`/`label`); `source` and `target` must reference node `id`s.\n75\t\n76\t## OUTPUT CONTRACT\n77\t\n78\tYou MUST produce THREE artifacts per iteration. The YAML-owned post_dispatch_validate step emits a `schema_mismatch` conflict event if any is missing or malformed.\n79\t\n80\t1. **Iteration narrative markdown** at `{state_paths_iteration_pattern}` (path pre-substituted for the current iteration number). Structure: headings for Dimension, Files Reviewed, Findings by Severity (P0/P1/P2), Traceability Checks, Verdict, Next Dimension.\n81\t\n82\t2. **Canonical iteration record recorded THROUGH THE APPEND GATEWAY** — never written to `{state_paths_state_log}` directly — the gateway is its only writer, and it refreshes that log from the ledger after authorizing, fencing, and receipting the record. The record MUST use `\"type\":\"iteration\"` EXACTLY, NOT `\"iteration_delta\"` or any other variant. The reducer counts records where `type === \"iteration\"` only; other types are silently ignored. Required schema:\n83\t\n84\t```json\n85\t{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":<n>,\"mode\":\"review\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-review\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\",\"run\":\"<run-id>\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"<dimension-or-focus>\",\"dimensions\":[\"...\"],\"filesReviewed\":[\"path:line\"],\"findingsCount\":<n>,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":<n>,\"P1\":<n>,\"P2\":<n>},\"findingsNew\":[],\"findingDetails\":[],\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"results\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"path:line\"],\"summary\":\"<one line>\"}]},\"newFindingsRatio\":<0..1>,\"sessionId\":\"<session-id>\",\"generation\":<n>,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"timestamp\":\"<ISO-8601>\",\"durationMs\":<n>,\"graphEvents\":[/* optional */]}\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\t### v2 Search Depth Output (when scopeClass is standard or complex)\n89\t\n90\tFor standard or complex review scope, set `\"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\":2` on the same iteration JSONL record and include these v2 fields in addition to the v1 fields above:\n91\t\n92\t- `reviewDepthApplicability`: `{scopeClass,enforcement,reason,evidenceRefs}` where `scopeClass` is `trivial`, `standard`, or `complex`; `enforcement` is `strict`, `warn`, or `skip`.\n93\t- `targetSelection`: `{selectedTargets,selectionReason,discoveryMethods,omittedHighRiskTargets,graphStatus,semanticSearchStatus,evidenceRefs}`. Name how targets were chosen, what high-risk targets were omitted, and whether graph/semantic search was available, unavailable, or partial.\n94\t- `searchCoverage`: `{requiredBugClasses,covered,ruledOut,deferred,blocked,graphCoverageMode}` where `graphCoverageMode` is `graph`, `graphless_fallback`, or `unavailable_blocked`.\n95\t- `searchLedger[]`: ledger rows with required `id`, `dimension`, `targetRefs`, `bugClass`, `disposition`, and `rationale`; include `hypothesis` or `invariant` (at least one); include `searchActions[]` with `{method,queryOrPath,result,evidenceRefs}`.\n96\t- Each ledger row needs exactly one disposition link: `linkedFindingId` for `finding` (must match an id in `findingDetails[]`), `ruledOutReason` for `ruled_out`, `deferredReason` for `deferred`, `blockedReason` for `blocked`, or `notApplicableReason` for `not_applicable`.\n97\t\n98\tTrivial-scope exemption: when `scopeClass` is `trivial` and `enforcement` is `skip`, `searchLedger` may be `[]`, but `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs` MUST cite proof that the target is trivial.\n99\t\n100\tCompact v2 example:\n101\t\n102\t```json\n103\t{\"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\":2,\"reviewDepthApplicability\":{\"scopeClass\":\"standard\",\"enforcement\":\"strict\",\"reason\":\"non-trivial target\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"path/to/file.ts:42\"]},\"targetSelection\":{\"selectedTargets\":[\"path/to/file.ts\"],\"selectionReason\":\"state transition producer\",\"discoveryMethods\":[\"direct_read\",\"exact_search\"],\"omittedHighRiskTargets\":[],\"graphStatus\":\"unavailable\",\"semanticSearchStatus\":\"partial\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"path/to/file.ts:42\"]},\"searchCoverage\":{\"requiredBugClasses\":[\"state_transition\"],\"covered\":[],\"ruledOut\":[\"state_transition\"],\"deferred\":[],\"blocked\":[],\"graphCoverageMode\":\"graphless_fallback\"},\"searchLedger\":[{\"id\":\"SL-001\",\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"targetRefs\":[\"path/to/file.ts\"],\"bugClass\":\"state_transition\",\"hypothesis\":\"state transition can skip validation\",\"searchActions\":[{\"method\":\"direct_read\",\"queryOrPath\":\"path/to/file.ts\",\"result\":\"guard present on all branches\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"path/to/file.ts:42\"]}],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\",\"rationale\":\"all branches call the guard\",\"ruledOutReason\":\"verified by direct read\"}]}\n104\t```\n105\t\n106\tLegacy unversioned records remain valid during rollout. Phase D validator behavior should warn on legacy shallow records and strictly enforce this shape only for explicit v2 records.\n107\t\n108\tRecord this single JSON object through the append gateway — do NOT `echo`/`>>` it into `{state_paths_state_log}` (the gateway is its only writer and refreshes it from the ledger). Write the one-line record to a temp file, then run:\n109\t\n110\t```bash\n111\tnode .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs \\\n112\t  --mode review \\\n113\t  --run-directory \"$(dirname '{state_paths_state_log}')\" \\\n114\t  --event-json <that temp file>\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\t`--event-json` must name the SINGLE-record file (the gateway `JSON.parse`s it whole), never the multi-line `{state_paths_delta_pattern}`. Exit `0` = the record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it; exit `2` = refused → STOP and name the failed check. Never fall back to a direct write.\n118\t\n119\t3. **Per-iteration delta file** at `{state_paths_delta_pattern}` (path pre-substituted, e.g. `deltas/iter-001.jsonl`). This file holds the structured delta stream for this iteration: one `{\"type\":\"iteration\",...}` record (same as the state-log append) plus per-event structured records (one per graphEvent, finding, classification, traceability-check, ruled_out direction). Each record on its own JSON line.\n120\t\n121\tExample delta file contents (one review iteration):\n122\t```json\n123\t{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":3,\"mode\":\"review\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-review\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\",\"run\":\"run-001\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"correctness\",\"dimensions\":[\"correctness\"],\"filesReviewed\":[\"path/to/file.ts:42\"],\"findingsCount\":7,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":2,\"P2\":5},\"findingsNew\":[],\"findingDetails\":[],\"newFindingsRatio\":0.41,\"sessionId\":\"session-001\",\"generation\":1,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z\",\"durationMs\":120000,\"graphEvents\":[]}\n124\t{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"R3-P1-001\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"cluster\":\"...\",\"file\":\"path:line\",\"title\":\"...\",\"iteration\":3}\n125\t{\"type\":\"classification\",\"detail\":\"...\",\"iteration\":3}\n126\t{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"...\",\"reason\":\"...\",\"iteration\":3}\n127\t```\n128\t\n129\t- When a finding sharpens one already recorded, set `\"refines\":\"<existing finding id>\"` on its row, and omit `refines` for a finding that is new.\n130\t\n131\tAll three artifacts are REQUIRED. The post_dispatch_validate step fails the iteration if any artifact is missing, malformed, or if the state-log append uses the wrong record type (`iteration_delta` etc.).\n132\t======\n133\t{\"effectiveConfig\":{\"kind\":\"cli-claude-code\",\"executable\":\"claude\",\"executableVersion\":\"sha256:f7c5093b9dd6560d08af28bc27b123fb55091deae3180ac39df199522da86815\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"medium\",\"serviceTier\":null,\"sandboxMode\":\"danger-full-access\",\"permissionMode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"sandboxEnforcement\":\"none\",\"effortApplied\":\"flag\",\"webSearch\":\"inherit\"},\"invocationFingerprint\":\"inv:6aac582bbbbda4710f8fc34315556791565f6cbb1df98ec9d3000093296ebaa7\"}\n134\t\n135\t{\n136\t  \"topic\": \"Review: specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub\",\n137\t  \"sessionId\": \"2026-11-21T21:52:56.000Z\",\n138\t  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n139\t  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n140\t  \"generation\": 1,\n141\t  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n142\t  \"migrationWindowEndsAt\": \"\",\n143\t  \"maxIterations\": 5,\n144\t  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.1,\n145\t  \"antiConvergence\": {\n146\t    \"minIterations\": 2,\n147\t    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n148\t    \"depthMode\": \"default\",\n149\t    \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\",\n150\t    \"divergent\": {}\n151\t  },\n152\t  \"expansiveDepth\": {\n153\t    \"maxDepth\": 3,\n154\t    \"maxChildrenPerNode\": 6,\n155\t    \"budgetSplit\": {\n156\t      \"depth1\": 0.5,\n157\t      \"depth2\": 0.35,\n158\t      \"depth3\": 0.15\n159\t    },\n160\t    \"maxFrontierNodes\": null\n161\t  },\n162\t  \"stopPolicy\": \"max-iterations\",\n163\t  \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n164\t  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n165\t  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 24,\n166\t  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n167\t  \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,\n168\t  \"specFolder\": \"specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub\",\n169\t  \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-21T21:52:56.000Z\",\n170\t  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n171\t  \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n172\t  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n173\t  \"executor\": {\n174\t    \"kind\": \"native\",\n175\t    \"model\": null,\n176\t    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n177\t    \"serviceTier\": null,\n178\t    \"sandboxMode\": null,\n179\t    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n180\t  },\n181\t  \"fanout\": {\n182\t    \"executors\": [\n183\t      {\n184\t        \"kind\": \"cli-mistral-vibe\",\n185\t        \"model\": \"deepseek-flash\",\n186\t        \"label\": \"vibe\",\n187\t        \"count\": 1,\n188\t        \"iterations\": 5\n189\t      },\n190\t      {\n191\t        \"kind\": \"cli-claude-code\",\n192\t        \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\",\n193\t        \"reasoningEffort\": \"medium\",\n194\t        \"configDir\": \"~/.claude-account2\",\n195\t        \"sandboxMode\": \"danger-full-access\",\n196\t        \"label\": \"claude2\",\n197\t        \"count\": 1,\n198\t        \"iterations\": 5\n199\t      }\n200\t    ],\n201\t    \"concurrency\": 2\n202\t  },\n203\t  \"mode\": \"review\",\n204\t  \"reviewTarget\": \"specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub\",\n205\t  \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n206\t  \"reviewDimensions\": [\n207\t    \"correctness\",\n208\t    \"security\",\n209\t    \"traceability\",\n210\t    \"maintainability\"\n211\t  ],\n212\t  \"reviewFocus\": \"The 8 commits main..HEAD on this branch that build the browser-use parent hub: the hub scaffold, the move of the Chrome DevTools and Aside modes into the hub, the Bladebro stealth-browser mode, advisor routing at both stages, nested sub-track support in system-spec-kit, and the end-to-end verification. Pure renames of moved spec packets are out of scope; review the edited and added files.\",\n213\t  \"resource_map_present\": false,\n214\t  \"reviewScopeFiles\": [\n215\t    \".skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs\",\n216\t    \".skilled/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs\",\n217\t    \".skilled/bin/compiled-routing-foundation.vitest.ts\",\n218\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/003-mcp-tooling/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json\",\n219\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/010-mcp-browser-use/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json\",\n220\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/010-mcp-browser-use/harness/build-artifacts.cjs\",\n221\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/010-mcp-browser-use/lib/policy-card.cjs\",\n222\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/010-mcp-browser-use/lib/registry-compiler.cjs\",\n223\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/010-mcp-browser-use/lib/router.cjs\",\n224\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/013-live-activation/activation/mcp-browser-use/fence-state.json\",\n225\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/013-live-activation/activation/mcp-browser-use/manifest.json\",\n226\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/013-live-activation/activation/mcp-tooling/manifest.json\",\n227\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/014-runtime-engine/lib/compiled-route.cjs\",\n228\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/014-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs\",\n229\t    \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/serving-closure.manifest.json\",\n230\t    \".skilled/bin/tests/compiled-route-admission.test.cjs\",\n231\t    \".skilled/bin/tests/compiled-route-rule-bound.test.cjs\",\n232\t    \".skilled/bin/tests/mcp-installers.test.cjs\",\n233\t    \".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.2.0.0.md\",\n234\t    \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/mcp-mutation-class-manifest.yaml\",\n235\t    \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/check-mcp-mutation-class.sh\",\n236\t    \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/check-mcp-mutation-class.test.sh\",\n237\t    \".skilled/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit\",\n238\t    \".skilled/skills/README.txt\",\n239\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/README.md\",\n240\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/ROUTER.md\",\n241\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/SKILL.md\",\n242\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/README.md\",\n243\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing/README.md\",\n244\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing/source.md\",\n245\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/README.md\",\n246\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/compiled-routing/2026-11-21--two-stage-replay--compiled/README.md\",\n247\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/compiled-routing/2026-11-21--two-stage-replay--compiled/results.csv\",\n248\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/compiled-routing/2026-11-21--two-stage-replay--compiled/skill-benchmark-report.json\",\n249\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/compiled-routing/2026-11-21--two-stage-replay--compiled/source.md\",\n250\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md\",\n251\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md\",\n252\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/description.json\",\n253\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/graph-metadata.json\",\n254\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/hub-router.json\",\n255\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/leaf-manifest.json\",\n256\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/leaf-scopes.json\",\n257\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/hub-routing/ambiguous-defer.md\",\n258\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/hub-routing/aside-browser-automation.md\",\n259\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/hub-routing/bladebro-stealth-browser.md\",\n260\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/hub-routing/chrome-devtools-browser-debug.md\",\n261\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/hub-routing/holdout-agentic-browser.md\",\n262\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/hub-routing/holdout-browser-inspect.md\",\n263\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/hub-routing/lighthouse-performance-audit.md\",\n264\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\",\n265\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\",\n266\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/README.md\",\n267\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/ROUTER.md\",\n268\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md\",\n269\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--app-running-rerun/README.md\",\n270\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-path-live/README.md\",\n271\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-path-live/source.md\",\n272\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/README.md\",\n273\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/agent-task/direct-task.md\",\n274\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/agent-task/session-continuation.md\",\n275\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/cli-lifecycle/account-status.md\",\n276\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/cli-lifecycle/help-fixture.md\",\n277\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/cli-lifecycle/install-version.md\",\n278\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/devtools-parity/console-network-capture.md\",\n279\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/devtools-parity/cookies-storage.md\",\n280\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/devtools-parity/dom-query-inspection.md\",\n281\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/devtools-parity/navigation-multi-tab.md\",\n282\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/devtools-parity/performance-timing.md\",\n283\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/devtools-parity/screenshot-pdf-capture.md\",\n284\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/intra-routing-recall/holdout-repl.md\",\n285\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/intra-routing-recall/holdout-troubleshoot.md\",\n286\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/intra-routing-recall/install.md\",\n287\t    \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/manual-testing-playb