{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EbffwrJEvhnGes2ZjoPaxW","type":"tool_result","content":"50:- A generic request to automate the browser with no tool named. The hub defers, so ask which mode the reader means.\n58:`hub-router.json` scores the request against its vocabulary classes. It then selects one `workflowMode`, an ordered bundle or a defer outcome. `mode-registry.json` maps that mode to its packet folder. The root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) maps the request to the selected mode's leaves and holds the fallback checklist, so read it before selecting a packet.\n60:Generic browser-automation phrasing defers instead of picking a mode. Debugging words go to Chrome DevTools, and so do Lighthouse and performance-trace requests. Deterministic signed-in proof goes to Aside. Agentic or stealth signed-in work goes to Bladebro.\n62:Take the mode from the compiled front door first, `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub mcp-browser-use --prompt \"<task>\"`, as the machine-router callout in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) says. Act on the decision: `route` loads its targets, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses. On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the `hub-router.json` routing above instead. Compiled routing is the default for this hub. Set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing fleet-wide, the explicit kill-switch.\n77:- **`defer`**: the outcome that asks for disambiguation when generic browser phrasing names no mode.\n128:- Never route generic browser-automation phrasing to a mode. Defer instead.\n105:> Follow the returned decision: `route` uses its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask for disambiguation, and `reject` refuses. On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the registry routing in `hub-router.json`. Set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing for every hub.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"a2b1ece4-22ed-475a-9943-954243b95096","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:33:56.964Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"50:- A generic request to automate the browser with no tool named. The hub defers, so ask which mode the reader means.\n58:`hub-router.json` scores the request against its vocabulary classes. It then selects one `workflowMode`, an ordered bundle or a defer outcome. `mode-registry.json` maps that mode to its packet folder. The root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) maps the request to the selected mode's leaves and holds the fallback checklist, so read it before selecting a packet.\n60:Generic browser-automation phrasing defers instead of picking a mode. Debugging words go to Chrome DevTools, and so do Lighthouse and performance-trace requests. Deterministic signed-in proof goes to Aside. Agentic or stealth signed-in work goes to Bladebro.\n62:Take the mode from the compiled front door first, `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub mcp-browser-use --prompt \"<task>\"`, as the machine-router callout in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) says. Act on the decision: `route` loads its targets, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses. On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the `hub-router.json` routing above instead. Compiled routing is the default for this hub. Set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing fleet-wide, the explicit kill-switch.\n77:- **`defer`**: the outcome that asks for disambiguation when generic browser phrasing names no mode.\n128:- Never route generic browser-automation phrasing to a mode. Defer instead.\n105:> Follow the returned decision: `route` uses its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask for disambiguation, and `reject` refuses. On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the registry routing in `hub-router.json`. Set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing for every hub.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{