{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGsVzN3vKRUoyF9GW1fZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018DJsEUUsofZyzCj2SCrXh9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro; wc -l $D/SKILL.md $D/references/*.md; sed -n 1,200p $D/references/install-and-verify.md","description":"Read Bladebro install-and-verify reference"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1930,"cache_read_input_tokens":159947,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1930},"output_tokens":69,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"c635e5b5-6083-402f-9b0b-a597efa83c12","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:35:32.859Z","request_id":"req_011ChGsVz8ubmY7BEzUvNm9Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018DJsEUUsofZyzCj2SCrXh9":{"command":"D=.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro; wc -l $D/SKILL.md $D/references/*.md; sed -n 1,200p $D/references/install-and-verify.md","description":"Read Bladebro install-and-verify reference"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018DJsEUUsofZyzCj2SCrXh9","type":"tool_result","content":"     194 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md\n      98 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/browser-lanes.md\n      91 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/cli-reference.md\n      88 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/install-and-verify.md\n      89 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/mcp-wiring.md\n     560 total\n---\ntitle: \"Bladebro Install and Verify\"\ndescription: \"Operator-gated install, the v4.8.2 pin check, SHA-256 verification against release sidecars, the agent and real-browser probes, and staged rollback. This file never installs anything itself.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"bladebro install\"\n  - \"bladebro doctor\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: reference\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n\n# Bladebro Install and Verify\n\nWhat to run, in order, once the operator says yes to an install. Every step is upstream documentation pinned to v4.8.2 and read 2026-11-21. None of it has run on this host.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nTurns the install and health check into steps with an expected output and a rollback, so a live run can be compared against this packet.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this file when `command -v bladebro` fails, when `bladebro doctor` reports a problem, or when the operator asks to install, update, verify or remove Bladebro.\n\n### Core Principle\n\nInstallation is an operator stop-for-yes. Without that yes, report the command and stop.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PREFLIGHT\n\n| Step | Command | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `command -v bladebro \\|\\| echo absent` | A path, or `absent` |\n| 2 | `node --version` | Node.js 14 or later for the npm launcher; a Chromium-family browser on the host |\n\n---\n\n## 3. INSTALL (OPERATOR YES REQUIRED)\n\n| Step | Command | Expected | Rollback |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3 | `npm install -g bladebro@4.8.2` | The package plus the native `bladebro-darwin-arm64` or `bladebro-darwin-x64` through optional dependencies; no postinstall script | `npm uninstall -g bladebro` |\n| 4 | `bladebro doctor` | Health pass, the data root (`~/.local/state/blade` or `~/.blade`), a browser found | Set `CHROME_PATH`, re-run |\n| 5 | `bladebro --version` | `4.8.2` | None |\n\nLeave optional dependencies enabled. Verify the resolved native binary against the release `.sha256` sidecar with `shasum -a 256 -c` before use. The v4.8.2 macOS digests recorded at authoring are arm64 `sha256:7324e502b1710f8fb0a073b1f71d3647266d986a50e7351cb4257ec4eb5d8fa8` and x64 `sha256:d839f5f8a8bed8f616e68029350b1c36f8bc12ee2a16deb32b6f7df93a5a36c3`. For higher assurance, prefer the standalone prebuilt binary plus its digest over npm.\n\n---\n\n## 4. PROBES\n\n| Step | Lane | Command | Expected |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6 | MCP | Load the `bladebro` manual in Code Mode, run `list_tools()` | Five tools: act, see, state, run, vision |\n| 7 | Agent browser | `bladebro see content <url> --json` | One object with `ok`, `is_error`, `text`; exit 0 |\n| 8 | Agent browser | `bladebro see model --json`, then `bladebro act click ...` | Refs returned, then a verdict |\n| 9 | Agent browser | `bladebro vision --marks --json` | `image_path` to a non-empty PNG |\n| 10 | Agent browser | `bladebro state tabs` | The open tabs |\n| 11 | Real browser, on request | `bladebro rb status --json` | The current selection and live state |\n| 12 | Real browser, on request | `bladebro rb use`, `bladebro rb profile` | Browser and profile chosen by the operator |\n| 13 | Real browser, on request | `bladebro rb on` (`clone` or `auto` on macOS) | Tools and refs work with page injection off |\n\nRe-verify every flag against the installed binary (`bladebro help --json`) before relying on captured output. Capture detection output fresh each session and redact cookie and credential values.\n\n---\n\n## 5. TEARDOWN AND ROLLBACK\n\n| Step | Command | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 14 | `bladebro rb off`, then `bladebro stop` | Returns to the agent browser and stops the daemon |\n| Rollback | `npm uninstall -g bladebro` | Remove the data root `bladebro doctor` reported only after confirming no needed named sessions remain |\n\nUpdating is also an operator decision: `npm update -g bladebro` for npm installs, `bladebro -u` for the standalone binary, with `bladebro --rollback` to restore the previous standalone binary.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`cli-reference.md`](./cli-reference.md): the commands the probes call.\n- [`browser-lanes.md`](./browser-lanes.md): the consent checklist for steps 11-13.\n- [`mcp-wiring.md`](./mcp-wiring.md): the manual step 6 loads.\n- Upstream `docs/setup.md` and the GitHub Releases page at `<url>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"25473696-9327-4c3c-9893-3fd4db40ccd6","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:35:33.748Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     194 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md\n      98 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/browser-lanes.md\n      91 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/cli-reference.md\n      88 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/install-and-verify.md\n      89 .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/mcp-wiring.md\n     560 total\n---\ntitle: \"Bladebro Install and Verify\"\ndescription: \"Operator-gated install, the v4.8.2 pin check, SHA-256 verification against release sidecars, the agent and real-browser probes, and staged rollback. This file never installs anything itself.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"bladebro install\"\n  - \"bladebro doctor\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: reference\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n\n# Bladebro Install and Verify\n\nWhat to run, in order, once the operator says yes to an install. Every step is upstream documentation pinned to v4.8.2 and read 2026-11-21. None of it has run on this host.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nTurns the install and health check into steps with an expected output and a rollback, so a live run can be compared against this packet.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this file when `command -v bladebro` fails, when `bladebro doctor` reports a problem, or when the operator asks to install, update, verify or remove Bladebro.\n\n### Core Principle\n\nInstallation is an operator stop-for-yes. Without that yes, report the command and stop.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PREFLIGHT\n\n| Step | Command | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `command -v bladebro \\|\\| echo absent` | A path, or `absent` |\n| 2 | `node --version` | Node.js 14 or later for the npm launcher; a Chromium-family browser on the host |\n\n---\n\n## 3. INSTALL (OPERATOR YES REQUIRED)\n\n| Step | Command | Expected | Rollback |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3 | `npm install -g bladebro@4.8.2` | The package plus the native `bladebro-darwin-arm64` or `bladebro-darwin-x64` through optional dependencies; no postinstall script | `npm uninstall -g bladebro` |\n| 4 | `bladebro doctor` | Health pass, the data root (`~/.local/state/blade` or `~/.blade`), a browser found | Set `CHROME_PATH`, re-run |\n| 5 | `bladebro --version` | `4.8.2` | None |\n\nLeave optional dependencies enabled. Verify the resolved native binary against the release `.sha256` sidecar with `shasum -a 256 -c` before use. The v4.8.2 macOS digests recorded at authoring are arm64 `sha256:7324e502b1710f8fb0a073b1f71d3647266d986a50e7351cb4257ec4eb5d8fa8` and x64 `sha256:d839f5f8a8bed8f616e68029350b1c36f8bc12ee2a16deb32b6f7df93a5a36c3`. For higher assurance, prefer the standalone prebuilt binary plus its digest over npm.\n\n---\n\n## 4. PROBES\n\n| Step | Lane | Command | Expected |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6 | MCP | Load the `bladebro` manual in Code Mode, run `list_tools()` | Five tools: act, see, state, run, vision |\n| 7 | Agent browser | `bladebro see content <url> --json` | One object with `ok`, `is_error`, `text`; exit 0 |\n| 8 | Agent browser | `bladebro see model --json`, then `bladebro act click ...` | Refs returned, then a verdict |\n| 9 | Agent browser | `bladebro vision --marks --json` | `image_path` to a non-empty PNG |\n| 10 | Agent browser | `bladebro state tabs` | The open tabs |\n| 11 | Real browser, on request | `bladebro rb status --json` | The current selection and live state |\n| 12 | Real browser, on request | `bladebro rb use`, `bladebro rb profile` | Browser and profile chosen by the operator |\n| 13 | Real browser, on request | `bladebro rb on` (`clone` or `auto` on macOS) | Tools and refs work with page injection off |\n\nRe-verify every flag against the installed binary (`bladebro help --json`) before relying on captured output. Capture detection output fresh each session and redact cookie and credential values.\n\n---\n\n## 5. TEARDOWN AND ROLLBACK\n\n| Step | Command | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 14 | `bladebro rb off`, then `bladebro stop` | Returns to the agent browser and stops the daemon |\n| Rollback | `npm uninstall -g bladebro` | Remove the data root `bladebro doctor` reported only after confirming no needed named sessions remain |\n\nUpdating is also an operator decision: `npm update -g bladebro` for npm installs, `bladebro -u` for the standalone binary, with `bladebro --rollback` to restore the previous standalone binary.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`cli-reference.md`](./cli-reference.md): the commands the probes call.\n- [`browser-lanes.md`](./browser-lanes.md): the consent checklist for steps 11-13.\n- [`mcp-wiring.md`](./mcp-wiring.md): the manual step 6 loads.\n- Upstream `docs/setup.md` and the GitHub Releases page at `<url>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018DJsEUUsofZyzCj2SCrXh9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
