{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGsWfNakLaKaSL7CpHje","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LxCTcfZKt15bAZTGsaB3jZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro; sed -n 18,98p $D/references/browser-lanes.md; grep -n \"R-SEC\\|NEVER\\|ALWAYS\\|stealth\\|detection\\|captcha\\|terms\" $D/SKILL.md | head -40","description":"Read browser lanes consent and SKILL rules"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2724,"cache_read_input_tokens":164041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2724},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"1520e343-298e-4d86-80f6-b2280c848800","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:35:43.558Z","request_id":"req_011ChGsWfCQVcfrFvMxfsMsD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LxCTcfZKt15bAZTGsaB3jZ":{"command":"D=.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro; sed -n 18,98p $D/references/browser-lanes.md; grep -n \"R-SEC\\|NEVER\\|ALWAYS\\|stealth\\|detection\\|captcha\\|terms\" $D/SKILL.md | head -40","description":"Read browser lanes consent and SKILL rules"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LxCTcfZKt15bAZTGsaB3jZ","type":"tool_result","content":"## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nNames the lane to pick and the gate in front of it, so an agent never reaches a signed-in profile by default.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this file when a request names a real browser, a signed-in profile, `rb`, attach, clone or a caller-owned browser.\n\n### Core Principle\n\nThe agent browser is the default. Every real-browser lane runs only on an explicit operator request, after the operator has chosen the profile and account.\n\n---\n\n## 2. AGENT BROWSER (DEFAULT)\n\nBladebro owns this browser and its dedicated profile. State can persist across orderly shutdowns.\n\n- Isolate a task from ordinary Bladebro data with a separate `BLADE_HOME` set before the CLI or MCP server starts.\n- Request an ephemeral profile with `BLADE_FRESH=1`.\n- Prefer this lane wherever stealth or a signed-in session is not required.\n\n---\n\n## 3. REAL-BROWSER LANES (`rb`, EXPLICIT REQUEST ONLY)\n\n```sh\nbladebro rb use          # select the browser install (rb use <id>, or --binary <path>)\nbladebro rb profile      # select the profile (rb profile <key>)\nbladebro rb status       # show the selection and live state (--json for machine output)\nbladebro rb on           # switch to the real-browser lane\n```\n\nThe real-browser lane uses the operator's Chromium-family binary and selected profile, runs on the operator's display, and turns off the driver's page injection layer. Page perception, refs and actions stay available.\n\n| Lane | What Bladebro does | Guidance |\n|---|---|---|\n| `auto` (default `rb` lane) | Attaches to a live, reachable debug endpoint, otherwise imports and uses a clone | Fine on macOS |\n| `clone` | Imports the profile into a Bladebro-owned copy that refreshes when the real browser writes newer logins, cookies or storage; the source stays open and untouched | Preferred on macOS |\n| `profile` | Launches on the live profile; the browser must be closed first | Never on a live branded Chrome 136+, which refuses remote debugging on its default data directory |\n| `attach` | Connects to an existing debug endpoint; the browser stays caller-owned and open when Bladebro detaches | Use whenever the browser must remain open |\n\nThe upstream table labels these values `rb mode`. Confirm the exact selection command with `bladebro help rb` on the installed binary before using it.\n\n`bladebro rb refresh` forces a re-import of a clone. `bladebro rb forget` removes the imported copy.\n\n---\n\n## 4. PAUSE AND SWITCH BACK\n\n```sh\nbladebro rb pause    # block input, navigation, downloads, collection and tab operations\nbladebro rb resume   # re-enable input\nbladebro rb off      # return to the agent browser\n```\n\nReads, waits and eval stay available while paused, so the operator can take control and the agent can still observe. Gate every mutation in a signed-in profile behind this pair. The CLI restarts its daemon on a lane change; MCP picks the change up on its next use.\n\n---\n\n## 5. CONSENT CHECKLIST\n\nBefore handing control to an `rb` lane:\n\n1. The operator asked for a real-browser lane in this request.\n2. The operator chose the profile and account.\n3. For a stealth run, the operator confirmed the target site's terms of service and access rules.\n4. Only one writer acts on that account or profile.\n5. Detection output is captured fresh, with cookie and credential values redacted.\n\nA `blocked:` verdict ends the task. Report it and stop.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`cli-reference.md`](./cli-reference.md): the tools each lane exposes.\n- [`install-and-verify.md`](./install-and-verify.md): the probe order for the agent and real-browser lanes.\n- Upstream `docs/browser-modes.md` at `<url>\n23:- The work needs stealth on a signed-in site, and the operator has authorized it under R-SEC-2\n33:- Evading CAPTCHAs, anti-bot walls or access controls against a site's terms (R-SEC-2 forbids it)\n39:The `mcp-browser-use` hub selects this packet when a request names Bladebro, a stealth browser, `rb attach` or agentic signed-in work.\n61:- **Neither works:** report the install command and hand the decision to the operator. Never install implicitly (R-SEC-3).\n102:Aside keeps deterministic signed-in work. Bladebro takes the complement: stealth on a signed-in site, `rb attach` to a caller-owned browser that must stay open, and agentic branching signed-in workflows.\n112:**R-SEC-1 signed-in profiles.** \"Default to the Bladebro-owned agent-browser profile; use `BLADE_HOME`/`BLADE_FRESH=1` for task isolation. Any real-browser (`rb`) lane requires an explicit operator request, and the operator must select the profile/account before control is handed over. Use `attach` whenever the browser must remain caller-owned and open; do not use `profile` on a live branded Chrome. Gate mutations behind `rb pause`/`rb resume` and keep consent-sensitive actions human-in-the-loop. Never pass `--account` to `aside mcp` or `aside repl`, and keep a single-writer lock per account/profile. Re-capture detection output each session and redact cookie/credential values.\"\n114:**R-SEC-2 stealth and site terms of service.** \"Treat stealth as operator-authorized only. Before enabling a real-browser lane on a target site, the operator must confirm the site's terms of service and access rules; do not use Bladebro to evade CAPTCHAs, anti-bot walls, or access controls where doing so breaches those terms or applicable law. A `blocked:` verdict is terminal — report it and stop; do not re-issue the action, swap fingerprints, or otherwise route around the challenge. Keep stealth usage and the pinned v4.8.2 benchmark claim in the packet changelog, and prefer the agent-browser lane where stealth is not required.\"\n116:**R-SEC-3 npm binary supply chain.** \"Installation remains an operator stop-for-yes owned by 006 — never install implicitly. Pin the exact version the packet was authored against (v4.8.2) and record its read date in the packet changelog. Leave optional dependencies enabled but verify the resolved native package's SHA-256 against the published release sidecars (`shasum -a 256 -c`) before use; for higher assurance prefer the standalone prebuilt binary plus digest over npm. Re-verify CLI flags against the installed binary before relying on captured output. Roll back with `npm uninstall -g bladebro`, and remove the doctor-reported data root only after confirming no needed named sessions remain.\"\n118:### ✅ ALWAYS Rules\n120:1. Run the detection order (`command -v bladebro`, then `bladebro doctor`) before the first Bladebro action in a session.\n128:### ❌ NEVER Rules\n141:4. A site's terms of service for a stealth run are unconfirmed.\n148:Work is complete when the transport and the lane are named with the reason for each, detection output was captured this session, every action's exit code or `ok` field was read, artifacts were checked on disk, the daemon or MCP process was closed, and every capability gap met was routed to its covering mode rather than claimed.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"64bdd74d-a7a0-4ab5-a646-36edbc0611c2","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:35:44.861Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nNames the lane to pick and the gate in front of it, so an agent never reaches a signed-in profile by default.\n\n### When to Use\n\nLoad this file when a request names a real browser, a signed-in profile, `rb`, attach, clone or a caller-owned browser.\n\n### Core Principle\n\nThe agent browser is the default. Every real-browser lane runs only on an explicit operator request, after the operator has chosen the profile and account.\n\n---\n\n## 2. AGENT BROWSER (DEFAULT)\n\nBladebro owns this browser and its dedicated profile. State can persist across orderly shutdowns.\n\n- Isolate a task from ordinary Bladebro data with a separate `BLADE_HOME` set before the CLI or MCP server starts.\n- Request an ephemeral profile with `BLADE_FRESH=1`.\n- Prefer this lane wherever stealth or a signed-in session is not required.\n\n---\n\n## 3. REAL-BROWSER LANES (`rb`, EXPLICIT REQUEST ONLY)\n\n```sh\nbladebro rb use          # select the browser install (rb use <id>, or --binary <path>)\nbladebro rb profile      # select the profile (rb profile <key>)\nbladebro rb status       # show the selection and live state (--json for machine output)\nbladebro rb on           # switch to the real-browser lane\n```\n\nThe real-browser lane uses the operator's Chromium-family binary and selected profile, runs on the operator's display, and turns off the driver's page injection layer. Page perception, refs and actions stay available.\n\n| Lane | What Bladebro does | Guidance |\n|---|---|---|\n| `auto` (default `rb` lane) | Attaches to a live, reachable debug endpoint, otherwise imports and uses a clone | Fine on macOS |\n| `clone` | Imports the profile into a Bladebro-owned copy that refreshes when the real browser writes newer logins, cookies or storage; the source stays open and untouched | Preferred on macOS |\n| `profile` | Launches on the live profile; the browser must be closed first | Never on a live branded Chrome 136+, which refuses remote debugging on its default data directory |\n| `attach` | Connects to an existing debug endpoint; the browser stays caller-owned and open when Bladebro detaches | Use whenever the browser must remain open |\n\nThe upstream table labels these values `rb mode`. Confirm the exact selection command with `bladebro help rb` on the installed binary before using it.\n\n`bladebro rb refresh` forces a re-import of a clone. `bladebro rb forget` removes the imported copy.\n\n---\n\n## 4. PAUSE AND SWITCH BACK\n\n```sh\nbladebro rb pause    # block input, navigation, downloads, collection and tab operations\nbladebro rb resume   # re-enable input\nbladebro rb off      # return to the agent browser\n```\n\nReads, waits and eval stay available while paused, so the operator can take control and the agent can still observe. Gate every mutation in a signed-in profile behind this pair. The CLI restarts its daemon on a lane change; MCP picks the change up on its next use.\n\n---\n\n## 5. CONSENT CHECKLIST\n\nBefore handing control to an `rb` lane:\n\n1. The operator asked for a real-browser lane in this request.\n2. The operator chose the profile and account.\n3. For a stealth run, the operator confirmed the target site's terms of service and access rules.\n4. Only one writer acts on that account or profile.\n5. Detection output is captured fresh, with cookie and credential values redacted.\n\nA `blocked:` verdict ends the task. Report it and stop.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`cli-reference.md`](./cli-reference.md): the tools each lane exposes.\n- [`install-and-verify.md`](./install-and-verify.md): the probe order for the agent and real-browser lanes.\n- Upstream `docs/browser-modes.md` at `<url>\n23:- The work needs stealth on a signed-in site, and the operator has authorized it under R-SEC-2\n33:- Evading CAPTCHAs, anti-bot walls or access controls against a site's terms (R-SEC-2 forbids it)\n39:The `mcp-browser-use` hub selects this packet when a request names Bladebro, a stealth browser, `rb attach` or agentic signed-in work.\n61:- **Neither works:** report the install command and hand the decision to the operator. Never install implicitly (R-SEC-3).\n102:Aside keeps deterministic signed-in work. Bladebro takes the complement: stealth on a signed-in site, `rb attach` to a caller-owned browser that must stay open, and agentic branching signed-in workflows.\n112:**R-SEC-1 signed-in profiles.** \"Default to the Bladebro-owned agent-browser profile; use `BLADE_HOME`/`BLADE_FRESH=1` for task isolation. Any real-browser (`rb`) lane requires an explicit operator request, and the operator must select the profile/account before control is handed over. Use `attach` whenever the browser must remain caller-owned and open; do not use `profile` on a live branded Chrome. Gate mutations behind `rb pause`/`rb resume` and keep consent-sensitive actions human-in-the-loop. Never pass `--account` to `aside mcp` or `aside repl`, and keep a single-writer lock per account/profile. Re-capture detection output each session and redact cookie/credential values.\"\n114:**R-SEC-2 stealth and site terms of service.** \"Treat stealth as operator-authorized only. Before enabling a real-browser lane on a target site, the operator must confirm the site's terms of service and access rules; do not use Bladebro to evade CAPTCHAs, anti-bot walls, or access controls where doing so breaches those terms or applicable law. A `blocked:` verdict is terminal — report it and stop; do not re-issue the action, swap fingerprints, or otherwise route around the challenge. Keep stealth usage and the pinned v4.8.2 benchmark claim in the packet changelog, and prefer the agent-browser lane where stealth is not required.\"\n116:**R-SEC-3 npm binary supply chain.** \"Installation remains an operator stop-for-yes owned by 006 — never install implicitly. Pin the exact version the packet was authored against (v4.8.2) and record its read date in the packet changelog. Leave optional dependencies enabled but verify the resolved native package's SHA-256 against the published release sidecars (`shasum -a 256 -c`) before use; for higher assurance prefer the standalone prebuilt binary plus digest over npm. Re-verify CLI flags against the installed binary before relying on captured output. Roll back with `npm uninstall -g bladebro`, and remove the doctor-reported data root only after confirming no needed named sessions remain.\"\n118:### ✅ ALWAYS Rules\n120:1. Run the detection order (`command -v bladebro`, then `bladebro doctor`) before the first Bladebro action in a session.\n128:### ❌ NEVER Rules\n141:4. A site's terms of service for a stealth run are unconfirmed.\n148:Work is complete when the transport and the lane are named with the reason for each, detection output was captured this session, every action's exit code or `ok` field was read, artifacts were checked on disk, the daemon or MCP process was closed, and every capability gap met was routed to its covering mode rather than claimed.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LxCTcfZKt15bAZTGsaB3jZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
