{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ct8VXvoATaBVV9ebXw9QK","type":"tool_result","content":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/real-browser/lane-on-clone.md:65:1. Roll back with `bladebro rb off` and `bladebro rb forget`.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/lane-off-and-stop.md:46:2. `bladebro rb forget`\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:2:title: \"BB-014 -- Uninstall and data root removal\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates the final uninstall for `BB-014`. It focuses on the package and its data root being gone after operator approval.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:7:# BB-014 -- Uninstall and data root removal\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:15:Plan step 14, second half. It runs only after the operator approves removing the package and the data root the doctor reported.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:27:- Objective: Remove the global package and the data root.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:31:- Expected signals: npm exits 0, the data root is gone and step 3 prints `absent`\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:33:- Pass/fail: PASS if the package and the data root are gone. FAIL if either remains.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:60:- **Pass**: the package and the data root are gone.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:11:The agent-browser lane works on macOS. Install, the digest pin, the health check, the MCP and Code Mode lane and every agent-browser probe passed. The real-browser probe failed: with the Aside browser binary and a cookie-only staged copy of Aside's signed-in profile, every read in the real lane exited 1 with `Chrome launch failed: no page target available`. It was not retried. The lane was rolled back. The uninstall waits for operator approval.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:40:The operator approved the install of `bladebro@4.8.2` pinned, with the rollback `npm uninstall -g bladebro` plus removing its data root. The answer is recorded in the packet `goal.md` before any step 3 output. Each command ran once from the repository root on macOS arm64 against `<url> Output went to a scratch folder outside the repository.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:42:The real-browser steps ran once after the operator lifted the agent-profile limit for one probe: the Aside browser binary, Aside's signed-in `Default` profile copied with `Login Data*`, `Web Data*` and `Affiliation Database*` left out so that only cookies and site storage remained, `clone` mode and example.com only. `profile` mode was never used.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:46:In the quotes below the home folder is shortened to `~` and the scratch folder to `<scratch>`. Long page text is cut where marked. No cookie name or value appears anywhere in this record.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:226:$ bladebro rb profile <scratch>/aside-cookie-profile/Default\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:227:profile set to `<scratch>/aside-cookie-profile/Default`\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:234:  profile  \"Default\" · <scratch>/aside-cookie-profile/Default\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:240:The profile was first pointed at Aside's live `Default` folder, then repointed to the cookie-only staged copy before the lane turned on. No import happened while it pointed at the live folder. The status labels the browser `Google Chrome (Chrome)` even with the Aside binary override.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:246:[realbrowser] importing Google Chrome profile `Default` (<scratch>/aside-cookie-profile/Default)...\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:253:  revert     `bladebro rb off` · wipe imported copy: `rb forget`\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:306:$ bladebro rb forget\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:332:SKIP. Blocker: removing the package and the data root `~/.local/state/blade` waits for operator approval. `bladebro` is still installed.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:77:The real-browser `rb` lanes (`auto`, `clone`, `profile`, `attach`, plus `pause`/`resume`, `off`, `forget`) run only on an explicit operator request:\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:86:`rb pause` blocks input, navigation, downloads, collection and tab work while the operator takes over; `rb resume` re-enables it, `rb off` returns to the agent browser and `rb forget` removes an imported clone. Lane detail is in `references/browser-lanes.md`.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/browser-lanes.md:3:description: \"The owned agent-browser default and the operator-requested real-browser rb lanes: auto, clone, profile and attach, plus pause, resume, off and forget, with macOS guidance, pinned to v4.8.2.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/browser-lanes.md:64:`bladebro rb refresh` forces a re-import of a clone. `bladebro rb forget` removes the imported copy.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"3d107cb3-cc79-4919-8243-31fc05b5b6fc","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:35:51.168Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/real-browser/lane-on-clone.md:65:1. Roll back with `bladebro rb off` and `bladebro rb forget`.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/lane-off-and-stop.md:46:2. `bladebro rb forget`\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:2:title: \"BB-014 -- Uninstall and data root removal\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates the final uninstall for `BB-014`. It focuses on the package and its data root being gone after operator approval.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:7:# BB-014 -- Uninstall and data root removal\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:15:Plan step 14, second half. It runs only after the operator approves removing the package and the data root the doctor reported.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:27:- Objective: Remove the global package and the data root.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:31:- Expected signals: npm exits 0, the data root is gone and step 3 prints `absent`\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:33:- Pass/fail: PASS if the package and the data root are gone. FAIL if either remains.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:60:- **Pass**: the package and the data root are gone.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:11:The agent-browser lane works on macOS. Install, the digest pin, the health check, the MCP and Code Mode lane and every agent-browser probe passed. The real-browser probe failed: with the Aside browser binary and a cookie-only staged copy of Aside's signed-in profile, every read in the real lane exited 1 with `Chrome launch failed: no page target available`. It was not retried. The lane was rolled back. The uninstall waits for operator approval.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:40:The operator approved the install of `bladebro@4.8.2` pinned, with the rollback `npm uninstall -g bladebro` plus removing its data root. The answer is recorded in the packet `goal.md` before any step 3 output. Each command ran once from the repository root on macOS arm64 against `<url> Output went to a scratch folder outside the repository.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:42:The real-browser steps ran once after the operator lifted the agent-profile limit for one probe: the Aside browser binary, Aside's signed-in `Default` profile copied with `Login Data*`, `Web Data*` and `Affiliation Database*` left out so that only cookies and site storage remained, `clone` mode and example.com only. `profile` mode was never used.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:46:In the quotes below the home folder is shortened to `~` and the scratch folder to `<scratch>`. Long page text is cut where marked. No cookie name or value appears anywhere in this record.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:226:$ bladebro rb profile <scratch>/aside-cookie-profile/Default\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:227:profile set to `<scratch>/aside-cookie-profile/Default`\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:234:  profile  \"Default\" · <scratch>/aside-cookie-profile/Default\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:240:The profile was first pointed at Aside's live `Default` folder, then repointed to the cookie-only staged copy before the lane turned on. No import happened while it pointed at the live folder. The status labels the browser `Google Chrome (Chrome)` even with the Aside binary override.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:246:[realbrowser] importing Google Chrome profile `Default` (<scratch>/aside-cookie-profile/Default)...\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:253:  revert     `bladebro rb off` · wipe imported copy: `rb forget`\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:306:$ bladebro rb forget\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/README.md:332:SKIP. Blocker: removing the package and the data root `~/.local/state/blade` waits for operator approval. `bladebro` is still installed.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:77:The real-browser `rb` lanes (`auto`, `clone`, `profile`, `attach`, plus `pause`/`resume`, `off`, `forget`) run only on an explicit operator request:\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:86:`rb pause` blocks input, navigation, downloads, collection and tab work while the operator takes over; `rb resume` re-enables it, `rb off` returns to the agent browser and `rb forget` removes an imported clone. Lane detail is in `references/browser-lanes.md`.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/browser-lanes.md:3:description: \"The owned agent-browser default and the operator-requested real-browser rb lanes: auto, clone, profile and attach, plus pause, resume, off and forget, with macOS guidance, pinned to v4.8.2.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/browser-lanes.md:64:`bladebro rb refresh` forces a re-import of a clone. `bladebro rb forget` removes the imported copy.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012ct8VXvoATaBVV9ebXw9QK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
