{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGsgkxx8zgn533UEmQY9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01377Ntmt43xGFqDpVade7XR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"P=specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub; sed -n 98,125p $P/006-verification/decision-record.md | cut -c1-400; grep -n \"expected\\|gold\\|Expected\" .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/hub-routing/holdout-agentic-browser.md | head","description":"Read MT-H04 gold change decision"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1321,"cache_read_input_tokens":197776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1321},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"2ae90126-02a0-4264-94ac-37d6bbd15ff3","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:38:00.379Z","request_id":"req_011ChGsgkj4uJ3arcUjMFybv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01377Ntmt43xGFqDpVade7XR":{"command":"P=specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub; sed -n 98,125p $P/006-verification/decision-record.md | cut -c1-400; grep -n \"expected\\|gold\\|Expected\" .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/manual-testing-playbook/hub-routing/holdout-agentic-browser.md | head","description":"Read MT-H04 gold change decision"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01377Ntmt43xGFqDpVade7XR","type":"tool_result","content":"Hub-routing holdout MT-H04, \"Have the browser sign into the staging portal on its own, click through the checkout flow, and save proof screenshots of every step it takes\", now defers. Its gold answer `mcp-aside-devtools` dates from the old hub, before Bladebro existed. The prompt mixes agentic wording (\"on its own\", which the new hub gives to Bladebro) with signed-in proof (Aside). The defer turns\n```\n\nOptions:\n```text\nGold to defer (Recommended)\nRoute it to Aside\nLeave the drift\n```\n\nAnswer:\n```text\nGold to defer (Recommended)\n```\n\n### Q004\n<!-- source: claude:84103bdd-4074-43a6-b7db-ab9ef93e3535:toolu_01Gdjm3BzLWEcosz9TQ9koMe:1 -->\n\nQuestion:\n```text\nBladebro 4.8.2 is still installed globally, with its data folder `~/.local/state/blade` (62 MB, created by this run). The plan's step 14 uninstalls it after your approval. Since attach mode now works with your Aside, do you want to keep it?\n```\n\nOptions:\n```text\nKeep it installed (Recommended)\nUninstall now\n```\n6:expected_intent: defer\n7:expected_resources: []\n8:expected_workflow_mode: defer\n9:expected_leaf_resources: []\n22:The prompt names no tool. It asks the browser to act by itself and to save signed-in proof of each step. Under `mcp-tooling` this gold routed to `mcp-aside-devtools`, because Aside was then the only browser mode for that work. `mcp-browser-use` adds Bladebro, and its router splits the two halves of this request: agentic work in a signed-in browser belongs to Bladebro, deterministic signed-in proof belongs to Aside. Bare agentic phrasing is discovery-only in `hub-router.json`, so the hub defers and asks the caller to name the outcome.\n24:The gold changed from `mcp-aside-devtools` to `defer` on 2026-11-21, by operator decision, when the first run under the new hub deferred. The prompt is unchanged.\n28:A plain autonomous-browser request is common. When it could belong to two modes, the hub must defer on purpose rather than guess, and the gold must say so.\n34:Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `MT-H04` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n39:- Expected execution process: run the command in section 3 from the repository root, read the JSON the router prints and its exit status, then judge them against the pass/fail criteria.\n40:- Expected signals: the router prints `action: \"defer\"` with no target","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"9397401c-d67b-4c2a-a496-52d57e4f493b","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:38:01.205Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Hub-routing holdout MT-H04, \"Have the browser sign into the staging portal on its own, click through the checkout flow, and save proof screenshots of every step it takes\", now defers. Its gold answer `mcp-aside-devtools` dates from the old hub, before Bladebro existed. The prompt mixes agentic wording (\"on its own\", which the new hub gives to Bladebro) with signed-in proof (Aside). The defer turns\n```\n\nOptions:\n```text\nGold to defer (Recommended)\nRoute it to Aside\nLeave the drift\n```\n\nAnswer:\n```text\nGold to defer (Recommended)\n```\n\n### Q004\n<!-- source: claude:84103bdd-4074-43a6-b7db-ab9ef93e3535:toolu_01Gdjm3BzLWEcosz9TQ9koMe:1 -->\n\nQuestion:\n```text\nBladebro 4.8.2 is still installed globally, with its data folder `~/.local/state/blade` (62 MB, created by this run). The plan's step 14 uninstalls it after your approval. Since attach mode now works with your Aside, do you want to keep it?\n```\n\nOptions:\n```text\nKeep it installed (Recommended)\nUninstall now\n```\n6:expected_intent: defer\n7:expected_resources: []\n8:expected_workflow_mode: defer\n9:expected_leaf_resources: []\n22:The prompt names no tool. It asks the browser to act by itself and to save signed-in proof of each step. Under `mcp-tooling` this gold routed to `mcp-aside-devtools`, because Aside was then the only browser mode for that work. `mcp-browser-use` adds Bladebro, and its router splits the two halves of this request: agentic work in a signed-in browser belongs to Bladebro, deterministic signed-in proof belongs to Aside. Bare agentic phrasing is discovery-only in `hub-router.json`, so the hub defers and asks the caller to name the outcome.\n24:The gold changed from `mcp-aside-devtools` to `defer` on 2026-11-21, by operator decision, when the first run under the new hub deferred. The prompt is unchanged.\n28:A plain autonomous-browser request is common. When it could belong to two modes, the hub must defer on purpose rather than guess, and the gold must say so.\n34:Operators run the exact prompt and command sequence for `MT-H04` and confirm the expected signals without contradictory evidence.\n39:- Expected execution process: run the command in section 3 from the repository root, read the JSON the router prints and its exit status, then judge them against the pass/fail criteria.\n40:- Expected signals: the router prints `action: \"defer\"` with no target","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01377Ntmt43xGFqDpVade7XR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
