{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QSyby1V6MQLhfwqjYbBXAw","type":"tool_result","content":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/README.md:193:Not with any documented isolation. Aside has no isolation flag. Keep one manual and one writer per account and profile. The multi-client isolation test that would settle the question has not run.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/mcp-wiring.md:67:No callable name for this manual has been observed on this host. Do not assume one.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/install-and-verify.md:14:What to run, in order, once the operator says yes to an install. Every step is upstream documentation pinned to v4.8.2 and read 2026-11-21. None of it has run on this host.\n---\nregistry modes ['mcp-chrome-devtools', 'mcp-aside-devtools', 'mcp-bladebro'] keys ['skill', 'version', 'resourceContractVersion', 'description', 'discriminator', 'advisorRoutingContract', 'modes']\nrouter modes ['mcp-chrome-devtools', 'mcp-aside-devtools', 'mcp-bladebro']\nleaf manifest keys ['modes', 'resourceContractVersion']\ndesc {'name': 'mcp-browser-use', 'description': 'Parent hub for three browser modes: mcp-chrome-devtools for Chrome DevTools inspection, debugging, Lighthouse audits and performance traces, mcp-aside-devtools for deterministic signed-in REPL proof, and mcp-bladebro for stealth and agentic browser work. workflowMode selects the packet through mode-registry.json and hub-router.json. mcp-code-mode is shared infrastructure and not a hub member.', 'version': '1.1.0.0', 'importance_tier': 'high', 'keywords': 'list', 'lastUpdated': '2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z'}\nversions reg 1.1.0.0 router 1.1.0.0","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"a4072815-5e79-4a96-b433-c553e6ac6228","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:38:09.997Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/README.md:193:Not with a