{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGswURxBKySzXmmhFPtB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R3YY1HSNWn9TZoRwm8xP4S","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog; sed -n 1,80p $D/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md | cut -c1-260","description":"Read Lighthouse feature catalog entry"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2203,"cache_read_input_tokens":237467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2203},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"77521157-ad1c-4377-a9a0-a4f91ef010d0","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:41:23.137Z","request_id":"req_011ChGswUGYCnWKGkkoARs5W","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01R3YY1HSNWn9TZoRwm8xP4S":{"command":"D=.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog; sed -n 1,80p $D/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md | cut -c1-260","description":"Read Lighthouse feature catalog entry"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R3YY1HSNWn9TZoRwm8xP4S","type":"tool_result","content":"---\ntitle: \"Lighthouse and Performance Trace (MCP)\"\ndescription: \"lighthouse_audit scores accessibility, SEO and best practices but excludes performance; Core Web Vitals and load timing come from the performance trace tools. Both run only in the MCP lane through Code Mode.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"lighthouse audit\"\n  - \"performance trace\"\n  - \"core web vitals\"\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# Lighthouse and Performance Trace (MCP)\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe Chrome DevTools MCP serves two audit families, and they answer different questions. `lighthouse_audit` returns Lighthouse scores, the failing audits and the DOM nodes they flag for accessibility, SEO, best practices and agentic browsing, and saves the full\n\nBoth families run in the MCP lane only. The `bdg` CLI ships no Lighthouse command, so a Lighthouse or trace request uses Code Mode even when `bdg` is installed.\n\n---\n\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\nCall the tools through `call_tool_chain()` with the manual namespace, for example `chrome_devtools_1.chrome_devtools_1_lighthouse_audit({ ... })`. Confirm each name with `list_tools()` or `tool_info()` before the first call, because the exposed tool set change\n\n- **Lighthouse audit.** Open the page with `new_page`, run `lighthouse_audit`, then read the scores and the flagged nodes. Read the saved report for the full audit list.\n- **Performance trace.** Start `performance_start_trace`, load or interact with the page, stop with `performance_stop_trace`, then pass a named insight from the result to `performance_analyze_insight`.\n- **Cleanup.** Close the pages the program opened in a `finally` block, as the session-cleanup leaf describes.\n\n---\n\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|------|-------|------|\n| `SKILL.md` | MCP | Lane choice: the CLI first, the MCP for capabilities the CLI does not ship |\n| `assets/utcp-chrome-devtools-manuals.md` | Config | Registered `chrome_devtools_1`, `chrome_devtools_2` and `chrome_devtools_live` manuals |\n| `../mcp-aside-devtools/references/discovery-fixture-2026-07-16.json` | Evidence | A `list_tools()` snapshot that lists `lighthouse_audit` and the three trace tools |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|------|------|------|\n| `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` | Manual playbook | Code Mode scenarios for the MCP lane |\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: MCP Parallel Instances\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md`\nRelated references:\n- [code-mode-invocation.md](../../feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/code-mode-invocation.md): Code Mode Invocation\n- [session-cleanup.md](../../feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/session-cleanup.md): Session Cleanup (MCP)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"ba3e8832-393e-4b1a-8124-0db7af4d1cb8","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:41:23.932Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\ntitle: \"Lighthouse and Performance Trace (MCP)\"\ndescription: \"lighthouse_audit scores accessibility, SEO and best practices but excludes performance; Core Web Vitals and load timing come from the performance trace tools. Both run only in the MCP lane through Code Mode.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"lighthouse audit\"\n  - \"performance trace\"\n  - \"core web vitals\"\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# Lighthouse and Performance Trace (MCP)\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe Chrome DevTools MCP serves two audit families, and they answer different questions. `lighthouse_audit` returns Lighthouse scores, the failing audits and the DOM nodes they flag for accessibility, SEO, best practices and agentic browsing, and saves the full\n\nBoth families run in the MCP lane only. The `bdg` CLI ships no Lighthouse command, so a Lighthouse or trace request uses Code Mode even when `bdg` is installed.\n\n---\n\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\nCall the tools through `call_tool_chain()` with the manual namespace, for example `chrome_devtools_1.chrome_devtools_1_lighthouse_audit({ ... })`. Confirm each name with `list_tools()` or `tool_info()` before the first call, because the exposed tool set change\n\n- **Lighthouse audit.** Open the page with `new_page`, run `lighthouse_audit`, then read the scores and the flagged nodes. Read the saved report for the full audit list.\n- **Performance trace.** Start `performance_start_trace`, load or interact with the page, stop with `performance_stop_trace`, then pass a named insight from the result to `performance_analyze_insight`.\n- **Cleanup.** Close the pages the program opened in a `finally` block, as the session-cleanup leaf describes.\n\n---\n\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|------|-------|------|\n| `SKILL.md` | MCP | Lane choice: the CLI first, the MCP for capabilities the CLI does not ship |\n| `assets/utcp-chrome-devtools-manuals.md` | Config | Registered `chrome_devtools_1`, `chrome_devtools_2` and `chrome_devtools_live` manuals |\n| `../mcp-aside-devtools/references/discovery-fixture-2026-07-16.json` | Evidence | A `list_tools()` snapshot that lists `lighthouse_audit` and the three trace tools |\n\n### Validation And Tests\n\n| File | Type | Role |\n|------|------|------|\n| `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` | Manual playbook | Code Mode scenarios for the MCP lane |\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: MCP Parallel Instances\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md`\nRelated references:\n- [code-mode-invocation.md](../../feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/code-mode-invocation.md): Code Mode Invocation\n- [session-cleanup.md](../../feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/session-cleanup.md): Session Cleanup (MCP)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R3YY1HSNWn9TZoRwm8xP4S","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
