{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGt99huxhMcsdenwb99g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The claude2 lineage ran all 5 iterations and ended **CONDITIONAL**: no P0, one P1 and 10 P2 advisories.\n\n**The P1 to fix:** the new hub's compiled router refuses any request containing the word \"forbidden\". The check is at `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/010-mcp-browser-use/lib/router.cjs:107`. The hub is served compiled by default and SKILL.md says a `reject` refuses. So \"debug the 403 Forbidden network requests in chrome devtools\" gets refused instead of going to Chrome DevTools. I confirmed this by running both `resolve.cjs` and the front door SKILL.md names, `compiled-route.cjs`. The likely fix is to reject only when \"forbidden\" is passed as a constraint, never on the prompt text, and add a 403 test case that must route to Chrome DevTools.\n\n**The P2 advisories:**\n- **Routing words:** the bare word \"aside\" is matched anywhere in the text, so \"Aside from that, run lighthouse\" also pulls in the Aside mode. With every mode weighted equally, any prompt that hits one keyword in each of two modes loads both.\n- **Bladebro safety:**\n  - The documented update command skips the version pin and checksum check.\n  - The checksum check covers the native binary but not the npm launcher that actually runs.\n  - The default `auto` lane can attach to any browser listening on the debug port, regardless of the profile the operator picked.\n- **Packet docs:**\n  - The parent `spec.md:51` says phase 005 has two unmet requirements; phase 005's own summary lists three.\n  - Two Bladebro references still say nothing has run on this host, although the live macOS run happened.\n  - The Lighthouse catalog entry points at a playbook with no Lighthouse scenario.\n- **Spec-kit sub-tracks:** the two-level limit and the rule for what counts as a sub-track are written out in about 8 separate places, and `create.sh` hardcodes its own limit. A symlinked folder at level 2 disappears without the warning level 1 gives.\n\n**What I didn't run:** the advisor CLI and `nested-subtrack.vitest.ts`, because both would write outside the lineage directory. Stage-one routing and the sub-track checks rest on reading the diffs and phase 005's recorded replays.\n\n**Two small record issues:**\n- One search-ledger row in iteration 5 links to the wrong finding id; the ledger is append-only, so the report notes it instead of rewriting it.\n- A leftover `.run-open.json` file is in the lineage directory.\n\nEach iteration file, delta and state record went through the append gateway, with the reducer run after each. The final record carries `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`, the lock is released, and no file outside the review directory changed. The full report is `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/claude2/review-report.md`.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:claude2"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1119,"cache_read_input_tokens":259876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1119},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"aa903b31-f3fb-40ab-ac99-ae325f67a471","timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:44:04.676Z","request_id":"req_011ChGt99YUmfNRi21mfJhBf"}
